{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00475",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.57,
      "end_seconds": 4.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "I mean, good evening, doctor, thank you for staying late."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 5.96,
      "end_seconds": 9.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "Right on time. Sit, please. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 10.96,
      "end_seconds": 14.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.79,
      "end_seconds": 24.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.34,
      "text": "It's pain in the lower right tummy. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.77,
      "end_seconds": 26.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.74,
      "end_seconds": 29.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "About... well, two weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.08,
      "end_seconds": 33.73,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "Right, how would you describe it, mild, moderate, severe?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.33,
      "end_seconds": 47.82,
      "duration_seconds": 13.49,
      "text": "Pretty moderate, if I'm being honest. And there's vomiting once as well, five days now. Hmm, I've also had a low fever. As for low fever, mild, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 48.62,
      "end_seconds": 52.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any constipation or blood in the stool?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.5,
      "end_seconds": 56.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "No, no constipation or blood in the stool."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.34,
      "end_seconds": 63.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "What about burning when passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 63.93,
      "end_seconds": 66.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "No, no burning when passing urine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 66.97,
      "end_seconds": 71.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice burning when passing urine. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.96,
      "end_seconds": 78.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.26,
      "end_seconds": 84.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. And hernia bulge, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.19,
      "end_seconds": 88.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "No, I haven't had any hernia bulge."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.64,
      "end_seconds": 90.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Have you had any diarrhoea or jaundice?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.01,
      "end_seconds": 94.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "No, no diarrhoea or jaundice."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.15,
      "end_seconds": 97.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "How about your heart, any problems like that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.33,
      "end_seconds": 100.08,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "No, that's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.22,
      "end_seconds": 103.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "Your breathing, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.7,
      "end_seconds": 105.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "No, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 106.64,
      "end_seconds": 110.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 111.05,
      "end_seconds": 111.75,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 120.7,
      "end_seconds": 126.47,
      "duration_seconds": 5.77,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.02,
      "end_seconds": 129.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "My sister has epilepsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 131.08,
      "end_seconds": 144.93,
      "duration_seconds": 13.85,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.7,
      "end_seconds": 147.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.82,
      "end_seconds": 153.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.23,
      "text": "What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.12,
      "end_seconds": 156.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Thin bones, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.55,
      "end_seconds": 158.25,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.54,
      "end_seconds": 163.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "I have arthritis in my knees, for nearly five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.9,
      "end_seconds": 167.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.01,
      "end_seconds": 168.87,
      "duration_seconds": 0.86,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.71,
      "end_seconds": 185.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.55,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.75,
      "end_seconds": 188.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "No, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.52,
      "end_seconds": 195.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.34,
      "end_seconds": 197.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "No, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 198.23,
      "end_seconds": 200.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.0,
      "end_seconds": 204.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Alendronate, 70 milligrams, once a week for my bones."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 205.84,
      "end_seconds": 212.53,
      "duration_seconds": 6.69,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the alendronate was 140 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 213.95,
      "end_seconds": 218.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 218.99,
      "end_seconds": 230.2,
      "duration_seconds": 11.21,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Paracetamol. I take it 650 milligrams, when needed for the knee pain. It's the not knowing that gets to me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.6,
      "end_seconds": 243.19,
      "duration_seconds": 12.59,
      "text": "I see. It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.72,
      "end_seconds": 245.18,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.51,
      "end_seconds": 248.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.89,
      "end_seconds": 250.82,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.58,
      "end_seconds": 252.52,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.39,
      "end_seconds": 257.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 257.89,
      "end_seconds": 268.48,
      "duration_seconds": 10.59,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Oxygen saturation is 98 percent, temp 38.2 degrees, BP is 117 over 78, pulse is 101 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.92,
      "end_seconds": 269.81,
      "duration_seconds": 0.89,
      "text": "Okay, noted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.81,
      "end_seconds": 273.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.8,
      "end_seconds": 275.83,
      "duration_seconds": 1.03,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.71,
      "end_seconds": 279.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Okay, bear with me a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.96,
      "end_seconds": 289.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Bowel sounds are present."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.29,
      "end_seconds": 291.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.62,
      "text": "Let me check your reflexes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.2,
      "end_seconds": 312.68,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "There's tenderness in the right lower part and it hurts when I let go suddenly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 315.68,
      "end_seconds": 334.58,
      "duration_seconds": 18.9,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. Right, here's what I'm thinking. This looks most like possible appendicitis. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I'd also keep a gastroenteritis in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.97,
      "end_seconds": 344.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.11,
      "text": "Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had pain in the lower right tummy for two weeks, moderate, and no jaundice."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.54,
      "end_seconds": 346.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 348.16,
      "end_seconds": 364.92,
      "duration_seconds": 16.76,
      "text": "Let's get an ultrasound of the abdomen, for right lower abdominal pain. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. I'm going to order a urine test, for abdominal pain. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.49,
      "end_seconds": 366.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.31,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 368.04,
      "end_seconds": 370.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Have you had any tests for this so far?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 371.73,
      "end_seconds": 378.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "I had blood tests done at another clinic last year. I don't have the report with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 379.95,
      "end_seconds": 397.22,
      "duration_seconds": 17.27,
      "text": "Please don't eat or drink anything until the surgeons have seen you. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. We'll refer you to the surgical team. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.91,
      "end_seconds": 399.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.75,
      "end_seconds": 407.77,
      "duration_seconds": 8.02,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if the pain gets sharper or spreads across the tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 408.29,
      "end_seconds": 409.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.61,
      "end_seconds": 419.49,
      "duration_seconds": 8.88,
      "text": "Come back today after the results. Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 419.91,
      "end_seconds": 424.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "So, I come back today after the results. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 424.7,
      "end_seconds": 429.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.62,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Good. Call the clinic if you need us in the meantime."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0072",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 430.06,
      "end_seconds": 434.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "Okay, thank you. I'll get started on all of that."
    }
  ]
}